But you have completely changed the meaning of of the code...
Now instead of finding the last \ (backslash) in a pathname its 
finding the first one...

Your problem is that the kernel has no strrchr available, or the code 
should be rewritten to do this a different way.  Since the 386 has an 
assembly strrchr in include/asm-i386/string-486.h then the other 
architectures should have this available.

